WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.120
If NGF keeps neurons alive, can extra NGF make a ganglion bigger without limit?

2
00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:15.183
Give a chick embryo extra NGF every day, through the period when its neurons

3
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:16.183
normally die.

4
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.290
Predict. No change?

5
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.750
More survivors? New ganglia in the wrong places?

6
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.290
Fibres invading every tissue?

7
00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:34.633
More of the neurons survive than normal.

8
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:38.733
Survivors also grow larger and sprout more fibres.

9
00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:41.113
But no neuron changes its type.

10
00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:48.447
In 1981, Hamburger, Brunso-Bechtold and Yip counted chick dorsal root ganglia across

11
00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:49.447
the death period.

12
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.447
NGF reduced the normal death.

13
00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.227
How do you know they were saved, not born?

14
00:00:59.327 --> 00:01:01.787
Count neurons and dying nuclei at several stages.

15
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.340
Mark dividing cells.

16
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.220
Then check that the neurons carry markers of their usual type.

17
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:14.530
Very early in the chick, extra NGF can also increase division in the primary

18
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.690
sympathetic ganglia.

19
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.280
That happens before sympathetic axons reach their targets.

20
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.020
The extra division is NGF acting as something other than a survival factor.

21
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:32.333
Now the limit. A survival factor cannot save a neuron that was never made.

22
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:37.037
Take a ganglion that has made 1,000 neurons, with none added.

23
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:40.377
Each needs one unit a day from a shared supply.

24
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:44.677
With 500 units a day, the target limits survivors.

25
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:47.937
With 3,000, the number made limits them.

26
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:54.137
In this ideal model, survivors are at most the smaller of the neurons made and how

27
00:01:54.137 --> 00:01:55.577
many the supply can support.

28
00:01:56.377 --> 00:01:58.437
It is a budget bound, not a dose law.

29
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.920
Extra factor raises the second term.

30
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.700
Acting as a survival factor, nothing raises the first.

31
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:12.190
Now a puzzle. Spread those 500 units evenly over all 1,000 neurons.

32
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.830
Predict. Every neuron gets half of what it needs.

33
00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:18.710
How many survive?

34
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:29.423
It depends. Every neuron is equally short, so all are at risk at once.

35
00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.596
Each death frees factor for the rest.

36
00:02:33.396 --> 00:02:36.196
But a neuron already committed to dying cannot use it.

37
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.660
So the count depends on timing.

38
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.400
Slow commitment and quick sharing leave close to 500.

39
00:02:43.633 --> 00:02:46.333
Fast commitment leaves far fewer, perhaps none.

40
00:02:47.393 --> 00:02:49.813
Equal sharing alone does not say how many survive.

41
00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:58.863
When supply is short, matching it means the factor ends up with some neurons, not

42
00:02:58.863 --> 00:02:59.863
spread over all.

43
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.603
Slow, random loss can get there.

44
00:03:03.743 --> 00:03:06.163
Competition that picks winners early is another route.

45
00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:11.873
In mouse sympathetic neurons, evidence supports a model of active competition.

46
00:03:12.983 --> 00:03:17.763
NGF raises its own receptor, TrkA, in the neurons that receive it.

47
00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:21.103
A neuron that gets a little more can take up still more.

48
00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:26.946
Strong signallers release two related factors, BDNF and NT-4.

49
00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:30.286
They act through another receptor, p75.

50
00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:34.906
They push neighbours with weak NGF signalling toward death.

51
00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:37.986
Winners are amplified, and losers are punished.

52
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.360
One caution. The ceiling holds only for the population measured.

53
00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.800
Limb motor neurons do not depend on NGF.

54
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:52.293
Takeaway: extra NGF saves neurons, but never more than were made.

55
00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.593
How many survive depends on how the factor is shared.
